        "title": "Minami-Tori-shima",
        "raw_score": 2.242657616476173,
        "source": "kg"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Wake Island (also known as Wake Atoll) is a coral atoll in the western Pacific Ocean in the northeastern area of the Micronesia subregion, 1,501 mi east of Guam, 2,298 mi west of Honolulu and 1,991 mi southeast of Tokyo. The island is an unorganized, unincorporated territory of the United States Minor Outlying Islands that is also claimed by the Republic of the Marshall Islands. Wake Island is one of the most isolated islands in the world and the nearest inhabited island is Utirik Atoll in the Marshall Islands, 592 mi to the southeast.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999954387944,
      "temperature": 0.9999999954387944,
      "expanded": false,
